WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.389 align:start position:0%
 
who doesn't love a walk through a dark  forest the sight of branches set against  the low moonlight looking like all  manner of dark and twisted claws  reaching out of the night to grab at you  every step brings with it the snap of a  broken twig that practically echoes  around you whenever a breeze rustles the  leaves on the trees you feel like  something might just be following you  moving through the forest towards you it  is easy to get lost in a force at night  after all that's why the children's song  warns us that if you go down to the  woods today you'd better not go alone  the image of a forest in the darkness  has inspired fear for generations from  fireside folk tales telling of wolves  and monsters lurking among the trees to  modern horror games about a tall  faceless man in the suits stalking you  through the woods and then of course  there's scp-060  otherwise known as the infernal occult  skeleton now despite the name as  cp060 is in actual fact a forest or at  least it's a forest to begin with a  picturesque grove of 17 tall white oak  trees spread out across eight acres of  land in rural northeast minnesota it  almost looks like something out of a  tourist brochure a beautiful stretch of  forest sitting under clear skies well  during the daytime anyway if you ever  find yourself hiking through a corner of  minnesotan forest that isn't in any of  the guidebooks then tread carefully you  might just stumble upon the demolished  ruins of a house that used to stand  among the trees out in seclusion and a  word of advice to you if you happen  across this place do not under any  circumstances stop walking for a smoke  break of course thanks to the good folks  at the scp foundation you're unlikely to  ever just wander your way into scp-060  more likely they'll administer you with  amnesics the foundation's patented  memory altering drugs and send you on  your merry way totally oblivious to the  huge hard to miss greenhouses containing  scp-060 beyond those glass walls you  might have caught glimpses of foundation  personnel watering the trees carefully  tending to each  scp-060 specimen maybe you saw them  gathering up leaves and pruning each  tree individually composting every part  of dead plant matter instead of leaving  the white oaks to grow freely and  perhaps you even noticed that not one  member of personnel was carrying a  lighter on their person nor a taser or  so much as a small box of matches  nothing that can start a fire or rather  you would remember seeing all that if  the amnestics hadn't already made you  forget but what's so special about these  trees  why would the scp foundation go to the  extent of housing a collection of white  oaks in greenhouses and meticulously  oversee their growth what is it about  these particular specimens that make  personnel so cautious about fire safety  and why on earth is  scp-060 a collection of trees referred  to by the nickname the infernal occult  skeleton well the answer to all those  questions becomes pretty apparent the  moment any of the  scp-060 oak trees catch fire and  something comes hurtling out of the  forest that something is known as  scp-060  alpha standing at just over two meters  tall the entity takes the form of an  adult human skeleton much more than just  a spooky scary collection of bones  scp-060 alpha is fully animate capable  of moving of its own accord without the  aid of muscles or a nervous system oh  and it also happens to be on fire move  aside ghost rider  scp-060 alpha is engulfed from skull to  toe bones in bright white flames burning  at a temperature of approximately 1500  degrees celsius or almost 3 000 degrees  fahrenheit for reference that's just shy  of the melting point of iron and hot  enough to grant a human being a quick  but agonizingly painful death granted  after a few seconds of that heat your  nerve endings would be scalded so maybe  you wouldn't feel that much pain but  1500 celsius is enough to burn the  moisture right out of your skin melt  your eyeballs and generally fry you to a  crisp in a matter of minutes if not  seconds good thing  scp-060 alpha isn't known for being  highly aggressive and hostile oh wait it  is ah  not good upon manifestation the burning  skeleton will attempt to do as much  damage as possible and usually to  whoever is closest it can appear at any  time and after as little as 20 grams  worth of one of the scp-060 trees is  burned as if being actively hostile and  burning hot enough to reshape metal  wasn't bad enough  scp-060-alpha has also shown itself to  be fiercely intelligent the entity seems  to retain knowledge whenever it  manifests and has gained a growing  familiarity with the layout of the  foundation site that contains the  scp-060 oaks the infernal occult  skeleton's methods of attack tend to  include throwing its entire body at  flammable materials however it will  avoid causing any damage to specimens of  scp-060  the skeletal entity can run at speeds up  to 50 miles per hour now that's almost  the same speed as a gazelle just  picturing anything traveling towards you  at that speed is horrifying let alone  something headed straight for you at  gazelle levels of speed while also on  fire it is this combination of speed and  heat that means  scp-060 alpha poses such a threat to  anyone close whenever it appears if left  unchecked the entity could easily cause  colossal and widespread forest fires and  property damage  interestingly any areas that scp-060  alpha does burn with its flames will  start to yield saplings of the  scp-060 oaks around six weeks after the  fire has stopped the foundation doesn't  allow these saplings to grow to full  size and instead pulls them from the  ground and disposes of them composting  the saplings to feed the other  scp-060 specimens luckily the biggest  strength of scp-060 alpha its flames  also happens to be its greatest weakness  it is possible to fight the fires of the  infernal occult skeleton by dowsing it  with water or any other materials  capable of dousing flames whether it's  sand or foam from a fire extinguisher of  course this is a lot hotter and harder  to put out than any ordinary smaller  scale fire but despite being a difficult  task it is not impossible about 500  liters of water should do the trick if  you've got a big enough bucket nearby  after that  scp-060 alpha will be weakened gradually  collapsing and turning into dust however  if another part of an scp-060 tree is  burned and the entity reappears it is  believed that this will be the same  infernal occult skeleton rather than a  new version of the bone-burning being so  we have a grove of oak trees that  manifest a flaming skeleton if they are  ever burned maybe that's not the  weirdest thing you'd see in a minnesotan  forest but wait there's something else  cast your mind back a few minutes and  you'll remember that we mentioned some  ruins the remains of a demolished house  that used to stand secluded among the  scp-060 white oak trees knowing that the  infernal occult skeleton can appear from  the oaks might make it obvious what  happened to this house but there's still  a story to be told here the house's  owner was a man by the name of jonathan  corhill now jonathan was something of an  odd man considered a bit of an eccentric  to some he preferred to spend his time  in solitude alone with his own thoughts  for company rather than mingling among  the rest of the world even his own  family noticed that mr corhill was  drifting away from them becoming a more  bitter nihilistic person in his old age  and choosing isolation over human  connection now sure loneliness doesn't  hold much appeal to everyone but  sometimes there are people who just  prefer being alone that might be what  drew jonathan corhill to a secluded  little house in the forests of minnesota  somewhere no one would bother him for  the most part the rest of the core hill  family adjusted to their eccentric  relatives behavior jonathan would have  rarely accepted visitors to his house in  the forest but he still kept in contact  with those who he'd been close with most  notably he'd regularly share phone calls  with his brother one christopher corhill  that is until something seemed to change  unexpectedly in the year 1996 on one of  their calls jonathan outright told  christopher to never contact him again  severing any ties with any remaining  family members and friends in the  outside world jonathan cut everyone off  living within his own bubble where he  could immerse himself in his unusual  interests according to christopher his  brother had seemed otherwise normal up  until a certain phone conversation but  jonathan had become obsessed with the  occult specifically he had embroiled  himself in the history of the victorian  era and certain supernatural practices  that had been undertaken in that time  period now whether christopher honored  his brother's wish to sever ties is  unknown a mail carrier would visit  jonathan's home in the woods not long  after their phone call maybe among the  envelopes this courier was delivering  what could have been a letter from  christopher or other members of the core  hill family begging their estranged  relative to come back to the world you  see even people who claim to prefer  being on their own sometimes need human  interaction talking to people and being  in the presence of friends and family  are hugely important factors in  maintaining a positive state of mental  health but what happens when someone  rejects that entirely and instead  becomes lost in their obsessive study of  the occult while the mail carrier was  the first to find out arriving at  jonathan corhill's woodland house the  courier found the place looking almost  skeletal a shell of the building that  had once stood in the forest according  to the locals the carrier had been sent  to deliver a notice to mr corhill  explaining that his house was being  foreclosed but it seemed someone or  something had beaten them to it a fire  had spread from the house's fireplace  quickly engulfing the entire structure  presumably with jonathan still inside it  wasn't until later that very same year  that jonathan corhill was officially  reported as a missing person case with  the local authorities any search that  was undertaken in an attempt to find him  uncovered next to no evidence of his  whereabouts to this day nobody knows for  certain if jonathan corhill is dead or  alive his whereabouts are unknown on the  surface it might be easy to make the  assumption that the infernal occult  skeleton reduced the reclusive old man  to nothing more than a cinder it  definitely seems plausible that jonathan  collecting firewood to keep himself warm  in his isolation accidentally chopped  down part of an  scp-060 oak put it in his fireplace and  called forth the vengeful flaming bones  but perhaps we shouldn't be so certain  after all core hill's house wasn't  entirely burned down despite the entity  normally trying to cause as much damage  as possible whenever it appears and on  top of that no human remains were found  in the house and the skeleton of  scp-060 alpha had to have come from  somewhere right  scp-060 offers a few warnings and not  just about the dangers of traveling  through the forest alone the appearance  of the flaming skeleton whenever the  scp-060 white oaks are burned could  serve as a reminder that we need to be  villagent in protecting the forests of  this world trees are one of our few  sustainable resources but for every one  we cut down or that catches fire it  takes years to regrow a replacement and  perhaps the third and final warning of  the infernal occult skeleton is simply  don't play with matches especially  around trees otherwise you might get  burned now go check out the plane that  never was scp-787  and scp-1440 the old man that kills all  living things he touches for more  morbidly fascinating scps

